(4) Any material applied, adopted or incorporated in any subsidiary legislation made under this Part or any online Code of Practice by reference under subsection (1) is to be treated for all purposes as forming part of the subsidiary legislation or online Code of Practice; and, unless otherwise provided in the subsidiary legislation or online Code of Practice, every amendment to any material incorporated by reference under subsection (1) that is made by the person or organisation originating the material is, subject to subsections (5) and (6), to be treated as being a part of that subsidiary legislation or online Code of Practice, as the case may be.

